pocket-motion-only: a mask is per-pixel coverage applied to every op that follows, which the software rasteriser can do by wrapping its framebuffer target and the PSP GE, ESP32 PPA, Symbian GLES2 and Vita GXM backends cannot — they draw ops, not coverage over ops. No upstream backend is taught the two ops; a stream carrying them stops at the first MASK_PUSH there.

0013 — `overflow-mask`: a node's children (and its own ground) clipped to the
node's outline — its rounded rectangle under its transform — rather than to
the axis-aligned bounding box `overflow-hidden` gives. Design and the tests'
red cases: `patches/0013-mask-op.design.md`.

What the patch adds, by file:

- `contracts/spec/spec.ts`, `gen-rust.ts`, `engine/core/src/spec.rs`
  (regenerated): `Overflow.Mask = 2`; `DRAW_OP.maskPush = 64`,
  `maskPop = 65` — the first codes in the range this project reserves
  (`src/vendor/draw-ops.ts`); `MASK_MAX_VERTS = 256`; the op format.
- `framework/compiler/tailwind.ts`: the `overflow-mask` token.
- `engine/core/src/layout.rs`: Mask lays out as Hidden.
- `engine/core/src/draw.rs`: Mask hit-tests as Hidden; `paint` emits
  SCISSOR (the AABB, as Hidden) then MASK_PUSH (the outline, clipped to the
  VIEWPORT — not the scissor, so a window's polygon does not depend on what
  it sits in and nested masks multiply exactly) before the node's ground,
  MASK_POP after its children; the ground under a mask is a plain box; a
  square-cornered axis-aligned window emits no mask and is `overflow-hidden`
  word for word. `mask_outline` flattens the corners by a radius table
  through the Taylor `sinf` every rotation already uses.
- `engine/core/src/raster.rs`: the POLY row walk is now `PolyScan`, shared
  by `poly()` and `mask_level()`, so a mask's coverage is POLY's by
  construction; `Masked`, a target over `&mut dyn RenderTarget` that scales
  every write by the top level's hits (`a * hits / 16`, POLY's own
  boundary expression) and multiplies levels under nesting; the dispatch
  loop (`render_ops`) wraps a plain target for the span up to the matching
  MASK_POP and re-enters itself once, whatever the nesting depth.
- `engine/core/src/damage.rs`: the two word counts and a bbox bound.
- `engine/core/src/tests.rs`, `damage.rs` tests: 14 tests. The ones that
  carry the claim: a white full-bleed child under a rotated square-cornered
  window is byte-identical to a white rotated box of the same geometry over
  54 size/angle cases (red with the level builder made binary); nested masks
  equal the product of the two single masks read back from their own
  renders (red with a minimum in place of the product).

2026-10-22, rebased onto 66caf4e5: main made the rasteriser generic over
`RenderResources` in place of `&Ui`, and `render_ops` takes it too; main's
`clip_fan` replaced `sutherland_hodgman`, and the outline is clipped by
`clip_poly`, the same passes (0008). `Overflow.Mask` is 2 beside main's new
`Contain` enum. The two draw-list walkers main added know MASK_PUSH
(2 + N) and MASK_POP (1).

`git apply` skips everything above the first `diff --git`.

